{{!-- CSV-only template (ETP-4899) — genuine comma-separated text, not the HTML/PDF page
      dumped verbatim. Same flat shape, columns and header label keys as
      template-excel.hbs (keep them in sync): the tree indent becomes a plain "Depth"
      column since CSV cannot express indentation, and "Type" (ETP-5663) is the
      account's ElementLevel label, or "Total" for a formula heading — see the Excel
      template for both and for the helpers the Type cell uses. Amounts
      print the raw dot-decimal value (no formatCurrency). Every text field goes through
      the canonical csvField (formula neutralization + quoting) — and every csvField
      call MUST be triple-stashed ({{{ }}}), never {{ }}: Handlebars HTML-escapes
      double-stash output by default, which turns csvField's own escaped `""` into
      `&quot;&quot;`, corrupting the CSV. --}}{{#with meta}}{{{csvField labels.hdrGroup}}},{{{csvField labels.hdrDepth}}},{{{csvField labels.hdrType}}},{{{csvField labels.hdrCode}}},{{{csvField labels.hdrName}}},{{{csvField labels.amount}}}{{#ifCond params.compareTo '===' 'true'}},{{{csvField labels.amount_ref}}}{{/ifCond}}
{{/with}}{{#each rows}}{{{csvField this.group}}},{{this.indent}},{{#if this.isFormula}}{{#ifCond this.elementlevel '===' 'E'}}{{{csvField @root.meta.labels.T}}}{{else}}{{{csvField (lookup @root.meta.labels this.elementlevel)}}}{{/ifCond}}{{else}}{{{csvField (lookup @root.meta.labels this.elementlevel)}}}{{/if}},{{{csvField this.value}}},{{{csvField this.name}}},{{this.amount}}{{#ifCond @root.meta.params.compareTo '===' 'true'}},{{this.amount_ref}}{{/ifCond}}
{{/each}}
